The Most Critical Topics to Master:
🔥 TOP PRIORITY:
Patient Load Process - This is the foundation of everything
Duplicate Management - Patient safety depends on this
Validation Process - Prevents data corruption issues
🎯 Key Takeaways for Your Preparation:
Patient Load is Iterative: It's not a one-time event. You'll do multiple loads, cleanup, validation cycles before going live.

Time Management: Start early! Duplicate cleanup can take much longer than expected (5 minutes per pair × thousands of pairs = significant time).

Validation is Critical: Epic emphasizes "validate more than you think is necessary" - this prevents major issues later.

Duplicate Rate Impact: A high duplicate rate affects patient safety, care quality, and user satisfaction. Clean it up before go-live.

Staffing Reality: Plan for dedicated resources. One person spending 25-50% time for setup, plus dedicated duplicate cleanup resources.
-------------------------------------


Based on the Epic Identity documentation, here are the tools available to eliminate duplicate records:

Epic Identity Duplicate Elimination Tools
1. Prevention Tools
Real-time Duplicate Checking: Automatically searches for potential duplicates when creating new patient records
Pre-save Validation: Flags potential duplicates before changes are saved to patient information
2. Detection Tools
Duplicate Configuration Records: Customizable matching algorithms that weight similarities between patient records
Identity Duplicate Algorithm: Epic's comprehensive matching system that includes:
Misspelled or flipped names
Transposed digits
Date of birth ranges
Multiple demographic field combinations
3. Analysis and Review Tools
Potential Duplicate Workqueues: Provides data integrity specialists with organized worklists of potential duplicates
Duplicate Reports: Detailed reports showing matching vectors, confidence weights, and common information
Identity Manager Activity: Shows all identification information including merges, overlays, and known non-duplicates
4. Resolution Tools
Automated Resolution
Auto-merge by Weight: Automatically merges records meeting specific confidence thresholds
Merge by Vector: Auto-merges based on specific combinations of matching criteria (regardless of overall weight)
Known Non-Duplicate by Vector: Automatically marks certain combinations as verified non-duplicates
Manual Resolution
Patient Merge Activity: Combines two patient records determined to be duplicates
Source patient (duplicate) merged into target patient (true record)
All accounts and coverages preserved
Target information overwrites source by default
Mark for Merge: Allows users to flag potential duplicates for review by data integrity staff
5. Correction and Recovery Tools
Patient Unmerge Activity: Restores mistakenly merged patient records to pre-merge state
Patient Contact Mover Activity: Moves encounters from incorrect patient record to correct patient record
Resolution Tasks: Provides checklist of items requiring manual review after unmerges or contact moves
6. Monitoring and Management Tools
Chart Correction Workspace: Manages all chart correction tasks and communications
Vector Rules: Advanced grouping system for faster, safer vector review
Overlay Resolution Reports: Assists in resolving encounters after patient unmerges
7. Workflow Integration Tools
Patient Lookup Enhancement: Customizable search fields to improve patient identification
Help Desk Integration: Built-in workflow for clinicians to report chart correction issues
In Basket Messaging: Communication system for task assignments and approvals
Key Features of These Tools:
Comprehensive Matching Logic
Name variations and misspellings
Date ranges and transposed numbers
Multiple demographic combinations
Cross-system duplicate detection
Flexible Automation
Configurable confidence thresholds
Custom vector combinations
Automated workflow routing
Bulk processing capabilities
Safety Features
Unmerge capability for mistakes
Resolution task tracking
Audit trails for all changes
Manual override options
Integration Capabilities
Works with downstream systems
Supports multiple ID types
Handles cross-system duplicates
Maintains referential integrity
The tools work together in a comprehensive workflow: Prevention → Detection → Analysis → Resolution → Monitoring, ensuring both proactive duplicate prevention and reactive duplicate cleanup capabilities.


